the following: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}\\,i+\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}\\,j \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\frac{1}{t})i+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(t)j \\\\  & =- \\frac{1}{t^{2}}\\,i+j \\\\ ‖{r}^{′}(t)‖ & =\\sqrt{{(\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t})}^{2}+{(\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t})}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{(- \\frac{1}{t^{2}})^2+1^2} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{\\frac{1}{t^{4}}+1} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{1 + \\frac{1}{t^{4}}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nNow, if  $f(x,y)=2 x y^{6},$ then we obtain \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(r(t)) & =2 \\left(\\frac{1}{t}\\right) t^{6} \\\\  & =2 t^{5}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can write the integral as \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{C}2 x y^{6}\\,\\text{d}s & ={\\int }_{1}^{2}f(r(t))\\,‖{r}^{′}(t)‖\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{2}\\left(2 t^{5}\\right)\\cdot\\left(\\sqrt{1 + \\frac{1}{t^{4}}}\\right)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{2}2 t^{3} \\sqrt{t^{4} + 1}\\,\\text{d}t.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we solve this using the substitution $u=t^{4} + 1,$ $\\text{d}u=4 t^{3}\\,\\text{d}t$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{1}^{2}2 t^{3} \\sqrt{t^{4} + 1}\\,\\text{d}t & =2{\\int }_{2}^{17}\\sqrt{u}\\cdot\\left(\\frac{1}{4}\\right)\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & ={\\int }_{2}^{17}\\frac{\\sqrt{u}}{2}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\left[\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot\\frac{2}{3}u^{3/2}\\right]_{2}^{17} \\\\  & =\\left[\\frac{u^{\\frac{3}{2}}}{3}\\right]_{2}^{17} \\\\  & =\\left(\\left(\\frac{\\left(17\\right)^{\\frac{3}{2}}}{3}\\right)\\right)-\\left(\\left(\\frac{\\left(2\\right)^{\\frac{3}{2}}}{3}\\right)\\right) \\\\  & =\\left(\\left(\\frac{17 \\sqrt{17}}{3}\\right)\\right)-\\left(\\left(\\frac{2 \\sqrt{2}}{3}\\right)\\right) \\\\  & =- \\frac{2 \\sqrt{2}}{3} + \\frac{17 \\sqrt{17}}{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535587 17592186045443 true] [17592186519922 1080 "25 \\sqrt{5}" 13194139535587 17592186045443 true] [17592186519922 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 13194139535587 17592186045443 true] [175