s of the end-points on the path.\n\nComputing ${r}^{′}(t)$ and $‖{r}^{′}(t)‖,$ we get the following: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}\\,i+\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}\\,j \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(t^{2})i+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(t)j \\\\  & =2 t\\,i+j \\\\ ‖{r}^{′}(t)‖ & =\\sqrt{{(\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t})}^{2}+{(\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t})}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{(2 t)^2+1^2} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{4 t^{2}+1} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{4 t^{2} + 1}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nNow, if  $f(x,y)=\\frac{6 x}{y},$ then we obtain \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(r(t)) & =\\frac{6 \\left(t^{2}\\right)}{t} \\\\  & =6 t.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can write the integral as \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{C}\\frac{6 x}{y}\\,\\text{d}s & ={\\int }_{1}^{2 \\sqrt{3}}f(r(t))\\,‖{r}^{′}(t)‖\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{2 \\sqrt{3}}\\left(6 t\\right)\\cdot\\left(\\sqrt{4 t^{2} + 1}\\right)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{2 \\sqrt{3}}6 t \\sqrt{4 t^{2} + 1}\\,\\text{d}t.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we solve this using the substitution $u=4 t^{2} + 1,$ $\\text{d}u=8 t\\,\\text{d}t$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{1}^{2 \\sqrt{3}}6 t \\sqrt{4 t^{2} + 1}\\,\\text{d}t & =6{\\int }_{5}^{49}\\sqrt{u}\\cdot\\left(\\frac{1}{8}\\right)\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & ={\\int }_{5}^{49}\\frac{3 \\sqrt{u}}{4}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\left[\\frac{3}{4}\\cdot\\frac{2}{3}u^{3/2}\\right]_{5}^{49} \\\\  & =\\left[\\frac{u^{\\frac{3}{2}}}{2}\\right]_{5}^{49} \\\\  & =\\left(\\left(\\frac{\\left(49\\right)^{\\frac{3}{2}}}{2}\\right)\\right)-\\left(\\left(\\frac{\\left(5\\right)^{\\frac{3}{2}}}{2}\\right)\\right) \\\\  & =\\left(\\left(\\frac{343}{2}\\right)\\right)-\\left(\\left(\\frac{5 \\sqrt{5}}{2}\\right)\\right) \\\\  & =\\frac{343}{2} - \\frac{5 \\sqrt{5}}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535587 17592186045443 true] [17592186519959 1080 "9 \\sqrt{5}" 13194139535587 17592186045443 true] [17592186519959 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 13194